t directly leads to Copper 6. The existing rules don't provide a path to Copper 6. So, without Record 5, there's no contradiction, but there's also no support for Copper 6. Therefore, the status would be undetermined (A) because there's no information to confirm or deny it.\n\nWait, but the original question is whether the removal of Record 5 changes the answer. The original answer was D (contradicted). After removal, since there's no rule preventing Copper 6, but no rule that enforces it, the answer would be A (undetermined). So the correct answer after the update is A.\n</think>\n\n{\"answer\": \"A\"}",
